==========================================================================================================================
PART 0 -- is the ring-versus-disc kinematic table available?
==========================================================================================================================
  The item points at Iodice et al. 2003 (A&A 404, 921) and Khoperskov.  Checked this session on the VizieR CfA
  mirror: J/A+A/404/921 returns no table -- that paper was never deposited at CDS.  The SDSS-based Polar Ring
  Catalogue (Moiseev et al. 2011, J/MNRAS/418/244) IS there but carries only positions, r magnitudes and a
  systemic velocity: no rotation curves.  Combes et al. 2013 (J/A+A/554/A11) adds CO spectra and systemic
  velocities, again no ring-versus-disc rotation.  So the ratio the item asks for cannot be measured from
  machine-readable data here.  What IS deposited is an HI survey of the Whitmore et al. 1990 Polar Ring
  Catalogue objects with 20% line widths (J/A+A/319/401), and that is what PART 2 uses.
  [PASS] 49a NOT RUNNABLE AS POSED -- the per-system ring and disc rotation velocities the item needs are not in any machine-readable archive reachable from here.  The polar-ring catalogues that ARE deposited carry photometry and systemic velocities only.  A data-availability result, not a null   (VizieR J/A+A/404/921 empty; J/MNRAS/418/244 and J/A+A/554/A11 carry no rotation velocities; J/A+A/319/401 carries HI 20% line widths and is used in PART 2)

